From 40e99991ff4f4e0ca46cd03123fa07a375af8053 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: briansp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 02:58:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] ggml-backend: order cross-device split-input copies after
 the destination's queued work

A device-to-device split input is copied by cpy_tensor_async on the SOURCE
backend's stream.  wait_before_overwrite() only makes the split backend's own
stream wait, so the copy was not ordered after work already queued on the
split backend - in particular the outbound copy of an earlier split's output,
which is issued on that backend's stream after the earlier split's event was
recorded.  When the allocator reused that output's region for the new input,
the incoming copy could overwrite it before it was copied out.

With per-split events on by default (GGML_SCHED_EVENTS) this showed up as
garbage prefill output with -sm layer on 2 GPUs and host experts
(--n-cpu-moe >= 29 on qwen4exp), where every MoE op of the second GPU's layers
runs on the first and activations cross devices for every layer.
GGML_SCHED_EVENTS=0 (a full synchronize instead) hid it.

Record a fresh event on the split backend right before such a copy and make
the source backend wait on it.  Same speed as the events-on default (37k
1146 vs 1114 t/s, 155k 1111 vs 1120), correct output.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ggml/src/ggml-backend.cpp | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-backend.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-backend.cpp
index 86a617ac5..108f21990 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-backend.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-backend.cpp
@@ -2691,6 +2691,17 @@ static enum ggml_status ggml_backend_sched_compute_splits(ggml_backend_sched_t s
                     copy_experts(first_id, last_id);
                 } else {
                     wait_before_overwrite();
+                    // A device-to-device input copy runs on the SOURCE backend's stream (cuda cpy_tensor_async), so it is
+                    // not ordered after work already queued on the split backend - including an outbound copy of an
+                    // earlier split's output, issued on this backend's stream AFTER that split's event was recorded.  With
+                    // the allocator reusing that output's region for this input, the copy could overwrite the output
+                    // before it was copied out.  Record a fresh event on the split backend and make the source wait on it.
+                    if (input_backend != split_backend && input_backend->iface.event_wait != NULL &&
+                        sched->events[split_backend_id][sched->cur_copy] != NULL &&
+                        !(input->buffer != NULL && ggml_backend_buffer_is_host(input->buffer))) {
+                        ggml_backend_event_record(sched->events[split_backend_id][sched->cur_copy], split_backend);
+                        ggml_backend_event_wait(input_backend, sched->events[split_backend_id][sched->cur_copy]);
+                    }
                     // A host-resident split input (a graph input or a small CPU-resident
                     // intermediate: `inp_pos`, `attn_inp_k_idxs`, ...) is re-copied on every split of a
                     // merged routed-MoE band (hundreds per pass).  The plain fallback below blocks the
